# Supabase project credentials — Dashboard → Project Settings → API.
#
# Copy this file to .env.local (gitignored by the `*.local` rule) and fill both
# values in. Vite reads them at dev-server start and at build time, so restart
# the dev server after changing them.
#
# Both are safe to ship to the browser: the anon key is the public half of the
# pair, and what it can reach is decided by row-level security. Never put the
# service_role key in a VITE_ variable — that one bypasses every policy.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-public-key

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ plans
#
# These are NOT for .env.local. They go in Vercel → Project → Settings →
# Environment Variables, and are read only by the functions in api/. None of
# them may start with VITE_, which would put them in the browser bundle.
#
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=   Supabase → Project Settings → API → service_role.
#                              Bypasses row-level security: server only.
# NOWPAYMENTS_API_KEY=         NOWPayments dashboard → Settings → API keys.
# NOWPAYMENTS_IPN_SECRET=      NOWPayments dashboard → Settings → IPN secret.
# SITE_URL=                    Optional. e.g. https://nexocards.vercel.app —
#                              where NOWPayments sends people back and posts
#                              payment updates. Defaults to the request's origin.
# NOWPAYMENTS_API_BASE=        Optional. https://api-sandbox.nowpayments.io/v1
#                              to test with the sandbox.
#
# This one IS public and does go in Vercel as a normal variable: set it to "on"
# once card / Apple Pay / Google Pay payments are enabled in NOWPayments, and
# the plans page will mention them.
# VITE_CARD_PAYMENTS=on
